  "name": "Nasi Lemak (Coconut Rice)",
  "text": "Nasi Lemak (Coconut Rice)\n\nPrep time: ?\n\nCooking time: ?\n\nTotal time: ?\n\nYield: ?\n\nStatus: untried\n\nIngredients\n\n2 cups basmati rice,\n\n½ cup water,\n\n1½ cups coconut milk,\n\n1 tbsp ginger root, 2 inches long (peeled and cut into julienne strips),\n\n2 star anise,\n\n1 cinnamon bark about 2” long,\n\n4 cardamom seeds,\n\n1 pandan leaf tied in a knot,\n\n½ tsp salt,\n\n1 tsp white sugar.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Wash and rinse the rice in a pot about three times or until the water runs clear.\n\n2. Add all the ingredients, including coconut milk, and stir.\n\n3. Cook on a medium heat, bringing it to the boil. Once boiled, turn down the heat, letting it simmer until the rice has gone fluffy.\n\n4. Stir it with a wooden or plastic spoon.\n\n5. Take off the heat and set aside for 10 minutes before serving.",
  "recipeYield": "?",
